  "claim_boundary": "This local development receipt runs the complete reference FGMRES recurrence for a 66-equation reduced-CSR fixture as a fixed, same-stream sequence of device-guarded HIP kernels. Four blocks per case execute the operator and reduction stages without a mid-recurrence host transfer. One case converges and a second case records restart then max-iterations; solution, residual-norm history, matvec accounting, terminal reason, and restart boundaries match the deterministic CPU reference. A canonical persisted checkpoint resumes from iteration one without replaying completed iterations and reaches the same one-shot terminal state. The fixed launch sequence, small reference dimension, small-fixture operator-derived Jacobi preconditioner, and restart-length limit are not a scalable production recurrence. It does not claim a production-scale multi-block operator, scalable production checkpoint implementation, production-scale preconditioner effectiveness or breadth, gfx1100 independent evidence, clean same-commit/wheel identity, signature, or performance.",
